cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use weft, please cite it as below."
title: weft
abstract: >-
  Single-writer actors, a level-triggered pool reconciler, and durable per-actor
  SQLite for the multiplayer fabric control plane.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Lee
    given-names: "K. S. Ernest (iFire)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/v-sekai-multiplayer-fabric/fabric-weft-plane"
keywords:
  - actors
  - control-plane
  - character
  - avatar
references:
  - type: standard
    title: "Characters and Avatars Technical Subgroup Charter"
    version: "0.1.0"
    date-released: 2025-09-24
    authors:
      - name: "Khronos 3D Formats Working Group, Characters and Avatars TSG (CATSG)"
    abstract: >-
      Charter of the Character and Avatars Technical Subgroup (CATSG) of the
      Khronos 3D Formats Working Group. weft adopts its terminology for the
      character domain: Character, Avatar, Persona, and Identity. weft renames the
      charter's "entity" (an avatar's controller) to "controller", because weft
      already uses "entity" for the runtime sim unit (the fabric entity packet).
